  "description": "The flame-throwing heat of this South Indian curry will have you screaming for more.",
  "notes": "Optional or for serving: Cooked rice to serve on the side\n\nOptional substitutions: tamarind pulp → lime juice; green small chiles → 1 serrano pepper\n\nNotes: This dish is meant to be hot and spicy, but can be tamed by adding less chiles. Adjust to taste. Dessicated coconut is unsweetened dried coconut. Don't substitute with sweetened coconut. If curry leaves are not available, simply omit. This dish is very forgiving, and the spices can be altered to taste.",
